    {
      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://woodcontractingchicago.com/services/whole-home-remodeling-chicago#faq",
      "name": "Frequently Asked Questions About Whole Home Remodeling in Chicago",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://woodcontractingchicago.com/services/whole-home-remodeling-chicago#webpage"
      },
      "mainEntity": [{
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does whole home remodeling take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most complete home remodeling Chicago projects take 8-16 weeks from start to finish. The timeline depends on the scope of work, number of rooms being remodeled, whether you're doing structural changes, permitting and inspection schedules, and material lead times. A typical whole home remodel touching kitchen, bathrooms, and finishes takes 10-14 weeks. We provide a detailed timeline with your proposal showing the construction sequence."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can I stay in my home during remodel?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "It depends on the scope of your home remodeling Chicago project. For remodels affecting kitchen and multiple bathrooms simultaneously, most families choose to move out temporarily since you'll be without essential facilities for weeks. For phased remodels where we complete spaces sequentially, staying is more manageable but still disruptive. We can structure the work to keep at least one bathroom functional if you're staying. We'll discuss living arrangements honestly during planning."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does whole home remodeling cost in Chicago?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Home remodeling Chicago costs typically range from $50,000 for focused multi-room updates to $200,000+ for complete gut remodels with high-end finishes. The main cost factors are square footage of your home, number of rooms being remodeled, kitchen and bathroom scope, structural or layout changes, finish quality selections, and mechanical system updates. A typical whole home remodeling project in Chicago costs $50,000-$100,000. We provide detailed, transparent proposals breaking down costs by space and category."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you provide design services for whole home remodel?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We partner with two exceptional local interior designers experienced in comprehensive Chicago home remodels. For whole home remodeling, professional design services are highly recommended to ensure cohesive flow between spaces, consistent material selections throughout, proper space planning, and a unified vision. You can work with our partner designers, your own designer, or we can help coordinate selections without formal design services."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What's involved in planning a whole home remodel?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Planning home remodeling Chicago requires comprehensive coordination. We start with assessing every space being remodeled, discussing your vision and priorities, creating detailed scope of work, developing construction sequencing, coordinating all material selections and lead times, planning for living arrangements during construction, and establishing realistic budgets and timelines. Good planning is critical for whole home projects to avoid delays and budget overruns."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Should I remodel everything at once or in phases?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Remodeling everything at once is typically more cost-effective and less disruptive long-term than phasing over years. Benefits include one mobilization and setup, coordinated material orders, consistent finishes throughout, single permit process, and getting it done rather than living in construction intermittently. However, budget constraints sometimes necessitate phasing. We can help you decide the best approach for your home remodeling Chicago project."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you handle permits for whole home remodeling?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, comprehensive home remodeling Chicago requires extensive permitting for structural, electrical, plumbing, mechanical work, and changes to living spaces. We handle all permit applications with the City of Chicago, coordinate required inspections throughout construction, ensure all work meets building codes, and manage the permitting timeline so it doesn't delay your project. Permit costs are clearly outlined in your proposal."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Can whole home remodeling include layout changes?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Absolutely. Whole home remodel is the ideal time for layout improvements: removing walls to open spaces, reconfiguring kitchens for better workflow, adding bathrooms or converting bedroom layouts, finishing basements into living spaces, and reimagining how rooms connect and flow. We work with structural engineers when needed for load-bearing walls and ensure all changes meet Chicago building codes."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What's your payment schedule for whole home projects?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Our standard payment schedule for home remodeling Chicago is: (1) Initial deposit upon contract signing (typically 20-30%), (2) Progress payments tied to completion milestones (demolition, rough-in, substantial completion of each major space), (3) Final payment upon project completion and your satisfaction. For large projects, payments are typically divided across 4-6 milestones. We never ask for full payment upfront."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will whole home remodeling increase my home value?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, comprehensive home remodeling Chicago typically provides strong return on investment, especially in desirable Chicago neighborhoods. Updated kitchens and bathrooms add the most value, but whole home consistency and modern systems are increasingly important to buyers. Most homeowners see 65-85% return on investment at resale, while immediately enjoying a completely transformed home. For families planning to stay long-term, the value is living in the home you want without moving."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
