      "@id": "https://woodcontractingchicago.com/service-area/logan-square-kitchen-bathroom-remodeling#faq",
      "name": "Common Questions About Remodeling in Logan Square",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://woodcontractingchicago.com/service-area/logan-square-kitchen-bathroom-remodeling#webpage"
      },
      "mainEntity": [{
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a kitchen remodel cost in Logan Square?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Kitchen remodels in Logan Square typically range from $15,000 to $80,000+ depending on scope, finishes, and how much original structure changes. Cosmetic updates run $15,000 to $22,000, mid-range remodels $22,000 to $50,000+, and full transformations with custom cabinetry $50,000 to $80,000+."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a Logan Square kitchen, bathroom, or whole-home remodel take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most Logan Square bathroom remodels run 4 to 6 weeks and kitchens 6 to 10 weeks. Whole-home historic renovations generally need 10 to 16 weeks. Older greystones and bungalows can add time once walls are open, which is why we plan the scope around what we expect to find."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a permit to remodel in Logan Square?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes, Chicago building permits are required for most kitchen and bathroom remodels that involve plumbing, electrical, or structural changes. We advise you on when a permit is needed and coordinate permit pull-through when the project scope calls for it. Permits typically take 2 to 4 weeks."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you have experience with my type of Logan Square home?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Very likely. We have remodeled the boulevard greystones and the cottages, bungalows, and flats throughout Logan Square. Share your address and we can tell you what we typically run into in that era of home."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a bathroom remodel cost in Logan Square?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Bathroom remodels range from $12,000 for powder room updates to $55,000+ for luxury primary bathrooms. Half baths typically cost $12,000 to $20,000, full bathrooms run $20,000 to $32,000+, and primary bathrooms with custom features cost $32,000 to $55,000+"
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What should I know about renovating a historic Logan Square home?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Older Logan Square homes commonly hide knob-and-tube wiring, galvanized plumbing, and plaster-and-lath walls, and greystones on the boulevards can carry historic-district review. We plan for these realities up front so the budget and timeline hold, and we protect the period detail worth keeping."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will my renovation increase my home's value?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We work year-round, though late fall through early spring often offers more flexible scheduling. For whole-home historic projects, permit and any historic-district review can drive the start date, so it helps to begin the consultation a couple of months ahead of when you want work underway."
          }
        }
