      "@type": "FAQPage",
      "@id": "https://woodcontractingchicago.com/service-area/lincoln-park-chicago-kitchen-bathroom-remodeling#faq",
      "name": "Common Questions About Remodeling in Lincoln Park",
      "isPartOf": {
        "@id": "https://woodcontractingchicago.com/service-area/lincoln-park-chicago-kitchen-bathroom-remodeling#webpage"
      },
      "mainEntity": [{
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a kitchen remodel cost in Lincoln Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Kitchen remodels in Lincoln Park typically range from $15,000 to $80,000+ depending on scope, finishes, and how much original structure or infrastructure has to change. Cosmetic updates run $15,000 to $22,000, mid-range remodels $22,000 to $50,000+, and full historic-kitchen transformations with custom cabinetry $50,000 to $80,000+."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a Lincoln Park kitchen, bathroom, or whole-home remodel take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most Lincoln Park bathroom remodels run 4 to 6 weeks and kitchen remodels 6 to 10 weeks. Whole-home historic renovations generally need 10 to 16 weeks. Older homes can add time once walls are open, which is why we plan the scope around what we expect to find."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a permit to remodel in Lincoln Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Most Lincoln Park kitchen and bathroom remodels that involve plumbing, electrical, or structural work require a Chicago building permit, and landmarked or historic-district blocks can add exterior review. As a licensed Chicago contractor, we tell you what your property needs and coordinate the approvals. City permits usually take about 2 to 4 weeks."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you have experience with my type of Lincoln Park home?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Very likely. We have remodeled Victorian greystones, brownstones, brick two- and three-flats, coach houses, and lakefront condos across Lincoln Park, from Webster Place and Park Lincoln to the blocks near DePaul and the park. Tell us your home and we can usually share what we typically find in that vintage."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a bathroom remodel cost in Lincoln Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Bathroom remodels in Lincoln Park typically range from $12,000 for powder rooms to $55,000+ for luxury primary baths, depending on finish level and what the older plumbing requires. Greystone and two-flat baths often need supply and drain updates behind the walls, which we fold into the plan."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What should I know about renovating a historic Lincoln Park home?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Older Lincoln Park homes commonly hide knob-and-tube wiring, galvanized plumbing, plaster-and-lath walls, and balloon framing, and landmarked blocks add exterior review. We plan for these realities up front so the budget and timeline hold, and we protect the period details worth keeping."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What's the best time of year to start a Lincoln Park renovation?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We work year-round, though late fall through early spring often offers more flexible scheduling. For whole-home historic projects, permit and any landmark review can drive the start date, so it helps to begin the consultation a couple of months ahead of when you want work underway."
          }
        }
      ]
    }
