      "mainEntity": [{
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a kitchen remodel cost in Hyde Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Kitchen remodels in Hyde Park typically range from $15,000 to $80,000+ depending on scope, finishes, and how much original structure changes. Cosmetic updates run $15,000 to $22,000, mid-range remodels $22,000 to $50,000+, and full transformations with custom cabinetry $50,000 to $80,000+."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How long does a Hyde Park kitchen, bathroom, or whole-home remodel take?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Most Hyde Park bathroom remodels run 4 to 6 weeks and kitchens 6 to 10 weeks. Whole-home renovations generally need 10 to 16 weeks. Pre-war greystones and co-ops can add time once walls are open, which is why we scope the work around what we expect to find."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do I need a permit to remodel in Hyde Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Yes. Most Hyde Park kitchen and bathroom remodels that involve plumbing, electrical, or structural work require a Chicago building permit, and landmarked blocks can add review of exterior changes. As a licensed Chicago contractor, we tell you what your property needs and coordinate the approvals. City review usually takes about 2 to 4 weeks."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Do you have experience with my type of Hyde Park home?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Very likely. We have remodeled the historic single-family homes and the vintage apartment buildings throughout Hyde Park. Tell us your home and we can usually share what we typically find in that vintage."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "How much does a bathroom remodel cost in Hyde Park?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Bathroom remodels in Hyde Park typically range from $12,000 for powder rooms to $55,000+ for luxury primary baths, depending on finish level and what the older plumbing requires. Greystone and pre-war co-op baths often need supply and drain updates behind the walls, which we fold into the plan."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "What should I know about renovating an older Hyde Park home?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Hyde Park homes are well-built, but the pre-war greystones, mansions, and co-ops commonly hide cast-iron plumbing, knob-and-tube wiring, and plaster over shifted framing. We plan for these realities up front so the budget and timeline hold, and we protect the original architecture worth keeping."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Will my renovation increase my home's value?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "We work year-round, though late fall through early spring often offers more flexible scheduling. For whole-home projects, and for co-op or condo buildings with board review, approvals can drive the start date, so it helps to begin the consultation a couple of months ahead."
          }
        }
      ]
